        "summary": "Zn–ligand chromophores sensitize Yb(III) NIR emission at 980 nm. Complex 2 shows the strongest NIR intensity among 2–5, attributed to two adjacent Zn(II) ions per Yb(III). Visible zinc/ligand-centered emission occurs near 464 nm.",
